§§ `22. Warrants`
-- applicant Commission, conditions, names officer and assistants, indicates subject, accompanied by copy of offences,
-- issued, exercised, produced to person, unoccupied, reasonable steps to inform, occupier informed, opportunity to be present,
-- copy left, premises secured
GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `Warrant Condition`
GIVETH A `Warrant Facts`
wcF MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, cs, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 5 10, YMD 2024 5 12, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

`condition 1` MEANS `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which have not been produced as required under section 20 or 21(5)(e)`
`condition 2` MEANS `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which the Commission may require under section 20, and that if required they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed`
`condition 3` MEANS `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents or goods within section 21, and that if notice is given under section 21(2) they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed`
`condition 4` MEANS `an investigation officer or authorised assistant has attempted to enter under section 21 but been unable to, and there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are documents or goods on the premises`

